      "title": "Lecturer, Electronic & Computer Engineering - School Of Engineering",
      "description": "Closing Date: 25/10/2026 Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button LECTURER, ELECTRONIC & COMPUTER ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic 03-05 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time Closing on 25 Oct 2026 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is This is a 2-year contract position as a Lecturer in the School of Engineering. What you will be working on Your responsibilities will include, but are not limited to, the following: Contributing to curriculum development, facilitating student learning, conducting assessments, and performing teaching-related duties for modules in Electronic and Computer Engineering, with a focus on embedded systems, programming, computer systems and infrastructure (networking, cloud, Linux, and cybersecurity), microelectronics, and artificial intelligence Identifying and spearheading opportunities for industry collaboration and partnership Participating in industry or consultancy projects to maintain professional relevance and industry alignment Supporting student development and growth in their educational journey What we are looking for A relevant degree in Electrical Engineering, Electronics Engineering, Computer Engineering, or Microelectronics, with at least 5 years of industry experience in areas such as product design/development/manufacturing, systems engineering, network/cloud infrastructure, or cybersecurity A passion for education and a strong commitment to nurturing, teaching, mentoring, and engaging with students Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to convey complex technical concepts effectively A self-driven and independent working style, coupled with strong collaborative abilities and a team-oriented mindset About Ngee Ann Polytechnic At Ngee Ann Polytechnic, our nine academic schools offer over 40 full-time diplomas to a growing student population of more than 15,000. As a public tertiary institution, internationally-recognised for its academic excellence and close industry links, NP prides itself on having a dedicated and professional teaching faculty, complete with campus facilities that are among the finest in the world.\n\nAn institution of higher learning, Ngee Ann Polytechnic believes in giving every student an enriching learning experience and every employee the opportunity to build a meaningful career.\n\nIf you are a self-starter with an innovative mind, a versatile person with the drive for all-rounded excellence, and a dedicated team player who shares our vision and values, we invite you to join our inspired team. You might also be interested in LECTURER / SENIOR LECTURER, SOFTWARE ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF INFOCOMM Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 18 Oct 2026 LECTURER, BIOMEDICAL ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 18 Oct 2026 LECTURER - COMMON BUSINESS PROGRAMME, SCHOOL OF BUSINESS & ACCOUNTANCY Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 18 Oct 2026 LECTURER / SENIOR LECTURER – EMOTIONAL INTELLIGENCE & GLOBAL CITIZENSH Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 25 Oct 2026 LECTURER, ELDERCARE - HMIS Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 25 Oct 2026 SERVICE-LEARNING CATALYST, LECTURER - HMIS Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 25 Oct 2026 LECTURER, AEROSPACE ENGINEERING (AVIONICS) - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 25 Oct 2026 LECTURER, AEROSPACE ENGINEERING (MECHANICAL) - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 25 Oct 2026 LECTURER, ELECTRONIC & COMPUTER ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 25 Oct 2026 APPLY NOW"
