    "https://www.careers.hrp.gov.sg/sap/bc/ui5_ui5/sap/ZGERCFA004/index.html?search-keyword=Ngee%20Ann%20Polytechnic#/JobDescription/17659190/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-b4c8-7a3b4afcf40d": {
      "title": "Lecturer / Senior Lecturer – Emotional Intelligence & Global Citizenship - Hmis",
      "description": "Closing Date: 15/11/2026 Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button LECTURER / SENIOR LECTURER – EMOTIONAL INTELLIGENCE & GLOBAL CITIZENSHIP - HMIS Ngee Ann Polytechnic 04-06 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time Closing in 1  day(s) 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is This is a 2-year contract position as a Lecturer/Senior Lecturer, Emotional Intelligence & Global Citizenship in the School of Humanities & Interdisciplinary studies. What you will be working on We are looking for an educator-facilitator who believes that developing the inner world of young people is an important part of preparing them for the outer world . This role sits at the intersection of emotional intelligence, interpersonal communication and global perspectives.  You will design and facilitate learning experiences that help young people better understand themselves, relate meaningfully to others, and think critically about the role they play in the world as agents of change.  As a facilitator of learning, you will guide students to discover their purpose and values, explore diverse perspectives on global issues, and translate their learning into meaningful community action. Your responsibilities will include, but are not limited to, the following: Facilitate engaging learning experiences for youths and adult learners focused on: Emotional Intelligence and Self-awareness Interpersonal Communication and Collaboration Creativity and Problem Solving Critical Thinking and Global Awareness Mentor youths (typically aged 16–20) through guided reflection, dialogue, experiential and project-based learning Design and facilitate learning experiences that connect classroom inquiry to real-world contexts, including community-based projects, civic dialogue or applied problem-solving Collaborate with a multidisciplinary team to continuously refine curriculum and learning experiences Provide pastoral care and holistic support for student development Able to teach at least one evening or weekends in the week Manage administrative work related to teaching and assigned projects Take on leadership roles in module delivery or project teams, , including study trips where required Undertake academic‑related administration, committee work, outreach activities, and ad‑hoc projects that support the School’s mission What we are looking for A relevant tertiary qualification, with at least 3 years of teaching and/or industry experience in Arts & Humanities, Business, Design, or related fields A strong belief in holistic education and the development of human skills, including emotional intelligence, communication, creative and critical thinking Experience in mentoring, coaching or working with youths Strong facilitation, interpersonal and communication skills Ability to design and facilitate engaging, interactive and reflective learning experiences Strong organisational skills, with attention to detail and the ability to manage multiple priorities A reflective practitioner who is open to learning, experimenting, and growing It would be an advantage if you have: Training or experience in areas such as emotional intelligence, youth development and/or global education Experience in facilitating civic dialogue or leading community-based learning projects About Ngee Ann Polytechnic At Ngee Ann Polytechnic, our nine academic schools offer over 40 full-time diplomas to a growing student population of more than 15,000. As a public tertiary institution, internationally-recognised for its academic excellence and close industry links, NP prides itself on having a dedicated and professional teaching faculty, complete with campus facilities that are among the finest in the world.\n\nAn institution of higher learning, Ngee Ann Polytechnic believes in giving every student an enriching learning experience and every employee the opportunity to build a meaningful career.\n\nIf you are a self-starter with an innovative mind, a versatile person with the drive for all-rounded excellence, and a dedicated team player who shares our vision and values, we invite you to join our inspired team. You might also be interested in ASSOCIATE LECTURER - STUDENT & YOUTH CARE SECTOR - HMIS Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing in 5  day(s) SERVICE-LEARNING CATALYST, LECTURER - HMIS Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 15 Nov 2026 LECTURER, CIVIL ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF DESIGN & ENVIRONMENT Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 15 Nov 2026 LECTURER, DESIGN  - SCHOOL OF DESIGN & ENVIRONMENT Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing in 5  day(s) LECTURER - SCHOOL OF DESIGN & ENVIRONMENT Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 08 Nov 2026 LECTURER, BIOMEDICAL ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 08 Nov 2026 LECTURER, ENGINEERING SCIENCE - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 08 Nov 2026 School of Infocomm - Lecturer (Common Infocomm Programme) Republic Polytechnic Closing in 2  day(s) LECTURER / SENIOR LECTURER – EMOTIONAL INTELLIGENCE & GLOBAL CITIZENSHIP - HMIS Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing in 1  day(s) APPLY NOW"
    },
    "https://www.careers.hrp.gov.sg/sap/bc/ui5_ui5/sap/ZGERCFA004/index.html?search-keyword=Ngee%20Ann%20Polytechnic#/JobDescription/17994912/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-b4c8-7e540d82940d": {
      "title": "Stakeholder Experience Partner - Hmis",
      "description": "Closing Date: 08/11/2027 Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button STAKEHOLDER EXPERIENCE PARTNER - HMIS Ngee Ann Polytechnic 04-06 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time Closing in 1  day(s) 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is This is a 2-year contract for Stakeholder Experience Partner position in the School of Humanities & Interdisciplinary Studies. You will play a pivotal role in supporting the establishment, operations, and growth of ENCORE (NP's flagship intergenerational hub). As part of a team supporting the centre, the role goes beyond administrative coordination to help develop operational systems, streamline workflows, coordinate diverse stakeholder engagements, and enable the successful delivery of strategic initiatives and programmes. The incumbent will need to navigate evolving requirements, exercise initiative, and work across multiple functions to build efficient and sustainable centre operations. What you will be working on Your responsibilities will include, but are not limited to, the following: Coordinate and manage end-to-end administrative and operational processes across ENCORE, ensuring smooth delivery of programmes, projects, events, and centre initiatives. Support the development and implementation of operating procedures, workflows, and documentation to establish effective and scalable centre operations. Manage multiple stakeholder touchpoints, including students, seniors, industry partners, community organisations, vendors, and internal departments. Track programme outcomes, maintain data repositories, prepare management reports, and support analysis to inform decision-making and reporting requirements. Coordinate procurement, budgeting administration, resource planning, and logistics to support centre activities and projects. Assist in developing communications materials, presentations, publicity content, and stakeholder engagement initiatives across various platforms. Identify opportunities for process improvement, digitalisation, and automation to enhance operational effectiveness, user experience, and service delivery. Provide secretariat support for meetings, working committees, and project teams, including scheduling, documentation, and follow-up on action items. Support the setup and operationalisation of new initiatives, programmes, partnerships, and events in a dynamic and evolving environment. What we are looking for At least 5 years of relevant experience in administration, operations, project coordination, or programme management. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities and stakeholders in a fast-paced and evolving environment. Strong organisational, coordination, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to work independently and exercise initiative. Proficient in Microsoft Office applications and digital collaboration tools. Experience in process improvement, workflow implementation, or operations optimisation will be an advantage. Adaptable, resourceful, and comfortable working in an environment where processes and structures are being established. Passion for supporting initiatives involving PMETs aged 50 and above, students, community partners, and industry stakeholders. About Ngee Ann Polytechnic At Ngee Ann Polytechnic, our nine academic schools offer over 40 full-time diplomas to a growing student population of more than 15,000. As a public tertiary institution, internationally-recognised for its academic excellence and close industry links, NP prides itself on having a dedicated and professional teaching faculty, complete with campus facilities that are among the finest in the world.\n\nAn institution of higher learning, Ngee Ann Polytechnic believes in giving every student an enriching learning experience and every employee the opportunity to build a meaningful career.\n\nIf you are a self-starter with an innovative mind, a versatile person with the drive for all-rounded excellence, and a dedicated team player who shares our vision and values, we invite you to join our inspired team. You might also be interested in TECHNICAL EXECUTIVE - CENTRE FOR ENVIROMENTAL SUSTAINABILITY Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 08 Nov 2027 Principal Manager (DX.IS) [Temp - 1 Year] Skills and Workforce Development Agency Closing on 06 Nov 2026 Assistant Manager, Procurement Singapore Land Authority Closing on 05 Nov 2026 Manager/Senior Manager, National AI Impact Programme (Administration) Skills and Workforce Development Agency Closing in 1  day(s) Asst. Manager / Manager - Programming Ops, Integrated Facilities Hub Sport Singapore Closing on 09 Nov 2026 Executive Officer, NSAS METI- HQ Closing on 06 Nov 2026 Senior/Assistant Director (Procurement) METI- HQ Closing on 06 Nov 2026 Assistant Manager/Manager, Procurement, Assurance & Corporate Excellen Sport Singapore Closing in 3  day(s) STAKEHOLDER EXPERIENCE PARTNER - HMIS Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing in 1  day(s) APPLY NOW"
