      "title": "Lecturer, Civil Engineering - School Of Design & Environment",
      "description": "Closing Date: 15/11/2026 Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button LECTURER, CIVIL ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF DESIGN & ENVIRONMENT Ngee Ann Polytechnic 03-05 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time Closing on 15 Nov 2026 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is This is a 2-year contract position as a Lecturer in the School of Design & Environment. What you will be working on Academic duties Develop and improve the content of modules you are assigned to teach and deliver. Be competent to conduct teaching and delivery of modules in classroom and online setting. Set and conduct assessment for the modules you are assigned. Lead in the integration of modules content, teaching and delivery to achieve the course objectives. Initiate and experiment with new pedagogies or learning technologies to enhance curriculum delivery. Non Academic duties Administrative and other duties to support the management of the school, diploma and modules Duties and responsibilities that may arises to support curriculum development and currency. Solve operational problems to ensure efficiency and effectiveness Supervise junior team members to ensure smooth operations What we are looking for Key Responsibilities Academic Delivery: Plan, develop, and deliver high-impact lectures, tutorials, and practical laboratory/studio sessions for both physical classrooms and online/hybrid learning environments. Curriculum & Module Leadership: Design and update module content across at least three core discipline areas to align with evolving industry standards and local regulatory frameworks. Student Mentorship: Guide full-time diploma students through their projects, industry attachments, and academic progression. Continuing Education (CET): Conduct evening classes (typically 6:00 PM – 10:00 PM) for working professionals enrolled in Part-Time Diplomas and short courses. Core Competencies & Subject Expertise Applicants must demonstrate competence to plan, develop, and teach at least three (3) of the following areas: AutoCAD and Autodesk (Revit / BIM) Civil Engineering & Structural Design Construction Management & Site Management Environmental Sustainability & Green Building Technologies Project Management Surveying Requirements & Qualifications Industry Experience: Minimum 3 years of demonstrated, hands-on professional experience in Building, Civil Engineering, Project Engineering, or Environmental Engineering, with a thorough working knowledge of current local legislations, codes, and professional practices. Technical & Software Proficiency: Strong command of industry-standard digital tools, including AutoCAD, Revit / BIM, 3D modeling software, and core enterprise office applications. Communication & Interpersonal Skills: Exceptional communication skills across written, oral, and graphic mediums, with the ability to convey complex technical concepts clearly. Passion for Teaching: An inherent drive and enthusiasm for education, mentorship, and fostering student success in both physical and digital learning spaces. About Ngee Ann Polytechnic At Ngee Ann Polytechnic, our nine academic schools offer over 40 full-time diplomas to a growing student population of more than 15,000. As a public tertiary institution, internationally-recognised for its academic excellence and close industry links, NP prides itself on having a dedicated and professional teaching faculty, complete with campus facilities that are among the finest in the world.\n\nAn institution of higher learning, Ngee Ann Polytechnic believes in giving every student an enriching learning experience and every employee the opportunity to build a meaningful career.\n\nIf you are a self-starter with an innovative mind, a versatile person with the drive for all-rounded excellence, and a dedicated team player who shares our vision and values, we invite you to join our inspired team. You 