      "title": "Lecturer, Biomedical Engineering - School Of Engineering",
      "description": "Closing Date: 08/11/2026 Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button LECTURER, BIOMEDICAL ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic 03-05 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time Closing on 08 Nov 2026 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is This is a 2-year contract position as a Lecturer, Biomedical Engineering in the School of Engineering. What you will be working on Your responsibilities will include, but are not limited to, the following: Spearhead and identify new opportunities and collaboration with industry. Undertake administrative tasks related to course management. Work on consultancy project to stay relevant in your profession. Lead or support applied R&D projects in collaboration with healthcare institutions and industry partners, focusing on assistive and rehabilitative technologies, wearable health monitoring systems, diagnostic devices, AI and data analytics in healthcare, 3D printing or rapid prototyping for medical applications Develop functional prototypes and demonstrators for teaching, research, and clinical validation. Support student development in the area of education. What we are looking for Relevant qualification in Biomedical Engineering, with at least 3 years of relevant industry experience in the areas of engineering design and development and/or manufacturing of medical technologies, including biomedical devices. Specifically, experiences in assistive/rehabilitation technology and/or wearable monitoring devices will be advantageous. Passionate about education and possess strong interest in nurturing, teaching, mentoring and interacting with students. Good communication and interpersonal skills. Self-driven, independent and possess readiness to work as a team. About Ngee Ann Polytechnic At Ngee Ann Polytechnic, our nine academic schools offer over 40 full-time diplomas to a growing student population of more than 15,000. As a public tertiary institution, internationally-recognised for its academic excellence and close industry links, NP prides itself on having a dedicated and professional teaching faculty, complete with campus facilities that are among the finest in the world.\n\nAn institution of higher learning, Ngee Ann Polytechnic believes in giving every student an enriching learning experience and every employee the opportunity to build a meaningful career.\n\nIf you are a self-starter with an innovative mind, a versatile person with the drive for all-rounded excellence, and a dedicated team player who shares our vision and values, we invite you to join our inspired team. You might also be interested in ASSOCIATE LECTURER - STUDENT & YOUTH CARE SECTOR - HMIS Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing in 5  day(s) LECTURER / SENIOR LECTURER – EMOTIONAL INTELLIGENCE & GLOBAL CITIZENSH Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing in 1  day(s) SERVICE-LEARNING CATALYST, LECTURER - HMIS Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 15 Nov 2026 LECTURER, CIVIL ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF DESIGN & ENVIRONMENT Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 15 Nov 2026 LECTURER, DESIGN  - SCHOOL OF DESIGN & ENVIRONMENT Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing in 5  day(s) LECTURER - SCHOOL OF DESIGN & ENVIRONMENT Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 08 Nov 2026 LECTURER, ENGINEERING SCIENCE - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 08 Nov 2026 School of Infocomm - Lecturer (Common Infocomm Programme) Republic Polytechnic Closing in 2  day(s) LECTURER, BIOMEDICAL ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 08 Nov 2026 APPLY NOW"
