    "https://www.careers.hrp.gov.sg/sap/bc/ui5_ui5/sap/ZGERCFA004/index.html?search-keyword=Ngee%20Ann%20Polytechnic#/JobDescription/16869692/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-b3e3-ea511a95740c": {
      "title": "Data & Governance Architect - Digital Services & Technology Office",
      "description": "Closing Date: 08/11/2026 Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button DATA & GOVERNANCE ARCHITECT - DIGITAL SERVICES & TECHNOLOGY OFFICE Ngee Ann Polytechnic 04-08 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time Closing on 08 Nov 2026 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is Responsible for the design, implementation, and governance oversight of the overall technical architecture of the Ngee Ann Polytechnic (NP) Enterprise Data and AI platform scalability This role ensures the platform’s technical architecture is scalable, secure, and aligned with enterprise standards while embedding data governance, lineage, and quality practices across all layers. This is a 2-year contract position with the Digital Services & Technology Office. What you will be working on Reporting to the Programme Manager of NP Data and AI platform, you will collaborate with various stakeholders, including respective schools and departments, and outsourced vendors) and will be responsible in the following areas of work: Architecture Lead the end-to-end architecture design for NP data Lakehouse and ensure detailed design and development is aligned with the enterprise architecture. Translate business requirements, including application resiliency requirements, governance requirements, into application architectural specifications. Design ingestion pipelines, medallion model (Bronze → Silver → Gold), and storage strategy in Delta Lake. Define standards for integrating structured/unstructured sources (DBs, APIs, SharePoint, PDFs). Architect and guide implementation of AI/ML and LLM integrations (Mosaic AI, Vector Search, Genie). Ensure system scalability, performance optimization, and resilience. Develop and maintain architecture guidelines, design patterns, and technology standards for the enterprise data platform. Review solution designs produced by Platform & Security Engineers and Data Engineers and vendors, ensuring consistency with architectural principles. Governance Design and implement RBAC, lineage, tagging, and classification using tools such as DataBricks Unity Catalog. Define encryption/tokenization standards and oversee secure views for Personally Identifiable Information access. Ensure platform with compliance frameworks (PDPA/GDPR, HIPAA, PCI DSS). Establish policies for data quality monitoring (Delta Live Tables expectations). Collaboration Work with Data Engineers to implement pipelines and secure data flows. Work with Data and AI Analyst to align stakeholders’ requirements with Lakehouse design and governance. Partner with Platform & Security Engineer to enforce encryption and key management. Collaborate with engineering, governance, ICT School, and business units to ensure architectural designs support teaching needs, analytics requirements, and institutional priorities. What we are looking for 4–8 years in data architecture, governance, or related fields. Proven experience in cloud-native data platforms (Databricks, Snowflake, BigQuery, or similar). Background in regulatory compliance and data governance frameworks. Skills & Certifications Certifications: Degree in Computer Science/Engineering or related discipline. Databricks Certified Data Engineer Professional / Architect, DAMA or CDMP certification in Data Management is a plus. Azure Solutions Architect / AWS Solutions Architect / GCP Architect is a plus. Technical Skills: Strong Spark, SQL, Delta Lake, and medallion architecture knowledge. Governance: Unity Catalog (lineage, RBAC, classification), metadata management. Cloud networking, IAM, and security integration. Other Skills: Relevant experience in GCC/GCC 2.0 is a plus. Strong understanding of data quality frameworks. Ability to define and enforce enterprise-wide governance policies. Attributes Strategic and meticulous. Able to bridge business, compliance, and technology needs. Strong leadership and stakeholder management. Risk-aware, compliance-focused, and adaptable About Ngee Ann Polytechnic At Ngee Ann Polytechnic, our nine academic schools offer over 40 full-time diplomas to a growing student population of more than 15,000. As a public tertiary institution, internationally-recognised for its academic excellence and close industry links, NP prides itself on having a dedicated and professional teaching faculty, complete with campus facilities that are among the finest in the world.\n\nAn institution of higher learning, Ngee Ann Polytechnic believes in giving every student an enriching learning experience and every employee the opportunity to build a meaningful career.\n\nIf you are a self-starter with an innovative mind, a versatile person with the drive for all-rounded excellence, and a dedicated team player who shares our vision and values, we invite you to join our inspired team. You might also be interested in SENIOR PLATFORM & SECURITY ENGINEER - DIGITAL SERVICES & TECHNOLOGY OF Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 08 Nov 2026 Senior Manager, Strategic Communications & Special Projects, NSAS METI- HQ Closing on 07 Nov 2026 Lead Engineer/Engineer, Programme Management Centre, PMG HTX Closing in 4  day(s) Assistant Director, Data Engineering & Architecture (1 year contract) Health Promotion Board Closing on 06 Nov 2026 [LTA-DPO] SNR MANAGER, PAYMENT TECHNOLOGY (MOTORING DIGITAL TRANSFORMA Land Transport Authority Closing on 05 Nov 2026 Senior Manager/Manager, WSH Technology, WSHI, OSHD MOM Closing on 07 Nov 2026 [12 months temp] Assistant Manager/Manager, Digital Platform Operation Sport Singapore Closing on 05 Nov 2026 Application Developer (1 year) MDDI Closing in 1  day(s) DATA & GOVERNANCE ARCHITECT - DIGITAL SERVICES & TECHNOLOGY OFFICE Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 08 Nov 2026 APPLY NOW"
    },
    "https://www.careers.hrp.gov.sg/sap/bc/ui5_ui5/sap/ZGERCFA004/index.html?search-keyword=Ngee%20Ann%20Polytechnic#/JobDescription/16869730/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-b3e3-ea511aa8140c": {
      "title": "Senior Platform & Security Engineer - Digital Services & Technology Office",
      "description": "Closing Date: 08/11/2026 Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button SENIOR PLATFORM & SECURITY ENGINEER - DIGITAL SERVICES & TECHNOLOGY OFFICE Ngee Ann Polytechnic 03-05 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time Closing on 08 Nov 2026 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is To design, build, secure, and operate the Enterprise Data & AI platform, ensuring it is reliable, cost-efficient, and compliant with enterprise governance standards. This role owns both the technical platform layer (clusters, jobs, CI/CD, monitoring) and the security layer (encryption, IAM, audit). This is a 2-year contract position with the Digital Services & Technology Office. What you will be working on Platform Operations Configure and maintain Enterprise Data and AI platform (e.g. Databricks workspaces, clusters, SQL warehouses, endpoints and workflows). Automate provisioning and deployments using Terraform, Databricks CLI, or APIs. Design and govern CI/CD frameworks used by Data Engineers for ETL/ML deployments, ensuring secure, compliant, and automated delivery workflows. Monitor platform usage, cost trends, and optimize performance of workloads. Maintain platform reliability and meet defined uptime and service-level objectives. Security Engineering Implement and maintain security controls for the enterprise data platform, including encryption, secrets management, and secure access patterns. Define and enforce role-based and attribute-based access policies across data assets and cloud compute resources. Configure secret scopes and secure service principal access. Monitor platform audit and activity logs to detect policy violations, anomalous access, and compliance risks. Ensure platform operations align with NP’s security, compliance, and regulatory requirements (e.g., IM8, NIST, GDPR. PDPA where applicable). Collaboration Work closely with Data Engineers, Governance Leads, and Analysts to ensure data pipelines, workflows, and products adhere to security and platform standards. Work closely with CI/CD team to integrate monitoring and alerting into observability stack. Advise leadership on platform performance and security posture and risks, optimisation opportunities, as well as compliance gaps. What we are looking for 3–5 years in cloud platform engineering or security engineering. Proven experience managing and securing large-scale data or ML platforms. Prior work in regulated industries (finance, healthcare, government) is a plus. Skills & Certifications Certifications: Degree or Diploma in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Information Technology or equivalent. Cloud security certs: Azure Security Engineer Associate / AWS Security Specialty / GCP Security Engineer. Infrastructure-as-code: Terraform or equivalent. Databricks Certified Administrator or Databricks Security Engineer is a plus Technical Skills: Cloud IAM, KMS, VPC/VNet, firewall/security groups. Encryption standards (AES, envelope encryption). CI/CD (Azure DevOps, GitHub Actions, Jenkins). Databricks platform administration (clusters, jobs, SQL warehouses, UC integration). Other Skills: Strong knowledge of monitoring/observability stacks (e.g. Azure Monitor). Incident response and audit log analysis. Experience in GCC/GCC2.0 is a plus. Attributes Reliability-focused and security-first mindset with attention to detail. Strong collaborator with engineering, governance, and leadership. Proactive in risk identification and mitigation. Balanced approach: performance and cost optimization while ensuring compliance. About Ngee Ann Polytechnic At Ngee Ann Polytechnic, our nine academic schools offer over 40 full-time diplomas to a growing student population of more than 15,000. As a public tertiary institution, internationally-recognised for its academic excellence and close industry links, NP prides itself on having a dedicated and professional teaching faculty, complete with campus facilities that are among the finest in the world.\n\nAn institution of higher learning, Ngee Ann Polytechnic believes in giving every student an enriching learning experience and every employee the opportunity to build a meaningful career.\n\nIf you are a self-starter with an innovative mind, a versatile person with the drive for all-rounded excellence, and a dedicated team player who shares our vision and values, we invite you to join our inspired team. You might also be interested in DATA & GOVERNANCE ARCHITECT - DIGITAL SERVICES & TECHNOLOGY OFFICE Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 08 Nov 2026 Senior Manager, Strategic Communications & Special Projects, NSAS METI- HQ Closing on 07 Nov 2026 Lead Engineer/Engineer, Programme Management Centre, PMG HTX Closing in 4  day(s) Assistant Director, Data Engineering & Architecture (1 year contract) Health Promotion Board Closing on 06 Nov 2026 [LTA-DPO] SNR MANAGER, PAYMENT TECHNOLOGY (MOTORING DIGITAL TRANSFORMA Land Transport Authority Closing on 05 Nov 2026 Senior Manager/Manager, WSH Technology, WSHI, OSHD MOM Closing on 07 Nov 2026 [12 months temp] Assistant Manager/Manager, Digital Platform Operation Sport Singapore Closing on 05 Nov 2026 Application Developer (1 year) MDDI Closing in 1  day(s) SENIOR PLATFORM & SECURITY ENGINEER - DIGITAL SERVICES & TECHNOLOGY OFFICE Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 08 Nov 2026 APPLY NOW"
    },
    "https://www.careers.hrp.gov.sg/sap/bc/ui5_ui5/sap/ZGERCFA004/index.html?search-keyword=Ngee%20Ann%20Polytechnic#/JobDescription/17565359/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-b3e3-e9919be0940c": {
      "title": "Lecturer, Engineering Science - School Of Engineering",
      "description": "Closing Date: 08/11/2026 Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button LECTURER, ENGINEERING SCIENCE - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic 03-06 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time Closing on 08 Nov 2026 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is This is a 2-year contract position as a Lecturer, Engineering Science in the School of Engineering. The role of a lecturer includes (1) Teaching & developing of modules including skills-based modules (2) Conducting training/courses for adult learners (3) Working on technology projects. What you will be working on Involvement in developing curriculum, facilitating student learning, conducting assessment and performing tasks for modules related to Diploma in Engineering Science, Common Engineering Programme and Diploma Plus Programme. Modules include but are not limited to: Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning Computer Vision and Deep Learning Autonomous Systems and IOT Data Analytics and Cloud Networks Data Security & Blockchain Generative AI Probability and Statistics Engineering Mathematics and Applied Physics Spearhead and identify new opportunities and collaboration with industry Work on industry or consultancy projects to stay relevant in your profession Lead or support applied R&D projects in collaboration with industry partners, focusing on Embodied AI, AI & Machine Learning and autonomous systems with applications spanning across robotics, advanced manufacturing, energy and transport. Support student development in the area of education Develop and delivery industry training programmes. What we are looking for Relevant qualifications in Engineering (e.g. Electronics,  Computer, Electrical, Mechanical, etc.)  with at least 5 years of relevant industry experience in product design/development/manufacturing or research and development Minimum 2 years of experience in emerging technological sectors such as embodied AI & Robotics, Machine Learning & Deep Learning or Data Analytics Passionate about education and possess strong interest in nurturing, teaching, mentoring and interacting with students Good communication and interpersonal skills Self-driven, independent and possess readiness to work as a team About Ngee Ann Polytechnic At Ngee Ann Polytechnic, our nine academic schools offer over 40 full-time diplomas to a growing student population of more than 15,000. As a public tertiary institution, internationally-recognised for its academic excellence and close industry links, NP prides itself on having a dedicated and professional teaching faculty, complete with campus facilities that are among the finest in the world.\n\nAn institution of higher learning, Ngee Ann Polytechnic believes in giving every student an enriching learning experience and every employee the opportunity to build a meaningful career.\n\nIf you are a self-starter with an innovative mind, a versatile person with the drive for all-rounded excellence, and a dedicated team player who shares our vision and values, we invite you to join our inspired team. You might also be interested in ASSOCIATE LECTURER - STUDENT & YOUTH CARE SECTOR - HMIS Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing in 5  day(s) LECTURER / SENIOR LECTURER – EMOTIONAL INTELLIGENCE & GLOBAL CITIZENSH Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing in 1  day(s) SERVICE-LEARNING CATALYST, LECTURER - HMIS Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 15 Nov 2026 LECTURER, CIVIL ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF DESIGN & ENVIRONMENT Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 15 Nov 2026 LECTURER, DESIGN  - SCHOOL OF DESIGN & ENVIRONMENT Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing in 5  day(s) LECTURER - SCHOOL OF DESIGN & ENVIRONMENT Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 08 Nov 2026 LECTURER, BIOMEDICAL ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 08 Nov 2026 School of Infocomm - Lecturer (Common Infocomm Programme) Republic Polytechnic Closing in 2  day(s) LECTURER, EN