    "https://www.careers.hrp.gov.sg/sap/bc/ui5_ui5/sap/ZGERCFA004/index.html?search-keyword=Ngee%20Ann%20Polytechnic#/JobDescription/18139302/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-b1c8-0d5229cd740b": {
      "title": "Associate Lecturer - Student & Youth Care Sector - Hmis",
      "description": "Closing Date: 15/11/2026 Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button ASSOCIATE LECTURER - STUDENT & YOUTH CARE SECTOR - HMIS Ngee Ann Polytechnic 03-99 year(s) Contract, Part-time Closing in 5  day(s) 21 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is We are seeking experienced professionals to join us as Associate Lecturers (ALs) to deliver adult Continuing Education and Training (CET) courses related to the student and youth care sector. Our courses are primarily designed for working adults and CET learners who are preparing for, entering, or currently working in student care, youth care and related social service settings. ALs will bring relevant professional expertise into the classroom, facilitate engaging and practice-oriented learning, connect theory to real-world practice, and support learners in developing knowledge and skills that can be applied in their work with children and youths. What you will be working on •\tDeliver and facilitate adult CET courses related to student and youth care •\tFacilitate engaging discussions, activities, case studies, simulations and group learning •\tConnect course concepts and frameworks to current industry practice •\tShare relevant professional experiences, examples and good practices •\tUse practical, learner-centred approaches that support adult learners with different levels of industry experience •\tSupport learners in applying concepts to workplace and practice-based situations •\tProvide feedback and guidance on learning activities and assessments, where applicable What we are looking for •\tRelevant degree or professional qualification in Social Work, Psychology, Early Childhood, Education, Youth Work, Social Services or a related discipline •\tRelevant industry experience in student care, youth care, social services, education, early childhood, community work or related fields •\tExperience in teaching, training, facilitation or professional development, preferably with adult learners •\tExperience delivering or supporting Continuing Education and Training (CET), WSQ or other adult learning programmes is an advantage •\tPractical experience working with children, youths, families, schools, student care centres or community organisations •\tStrong communication, facilitation and presentation skills •\tAbility to translate professional knowledge and industry experience into engaging, practical learning experiences •\tACTA, ACLP or an equivalent adult training qualification is preferred •\tA passion for developing working adults and future practitioners in the student and youth care sector We are particularly interested in hearing from professionals such as: •\tStudent Care Professionals •\tYouth Workers •\tSocial Workers •\tPsychologists •\tCounsellors •\tEducators and Teachers •\tEarly Childhood Professionals •\tSocial Service Practitioners •\tCommunity Practitioners •\tExperienced Trainers and Adult Educators This is an opportunity to share your industry knowledge and professional experience with working adults who are developing their capabilities for the student and youth care sector. You will contribute to applied, practice-oriented learning and help learners connect classroom concepts with the realities of working with children, youths, families and communities.  If you have strong industry experience, enjoy facilitating adult learning, and are passionate about developing practitioners in student and youth care, we would like to hear from you. About Ngee Ann Polytechnic At Ngee Ann Polytechnic, our nine academic schools offer over 40 full-time diplomas to a growing student population of more than 15,000. As a public tertiary institution, internationally-recognised for its academic excellence and close industry links, NP prides itself on having a dedicated and professional teaching faculty, complete with campus facilities that are among the finest in the world.\n\nAn institution of higher learning, Ngee Ann Polytechnic believes in giving every student an enriching learning experience and every employee the opportunity to build a meaningful career.\n\nIf you are a self-starter with an innovative mind, a versatile person with the drive for all-rounded excellence, and a dedicated team player who shares our vision and values, we invite you to join our inspired team. You might also be interested in LECTURER / SENIOR LECTURER – EMOTIONAL INTELLIGENCE & GLOBAL CITIZENSH Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing in 1  day(s) SERVICE-LEARNING CATALYST, LECTURER - HMIS Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 15 Nov 2026 LECTURER, CIVIL ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF DESIGN & ENVIRONMENT Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 15 Nov 2026 LECTURER, DESIGN  - SCHOOL OF DESIGN & ENVIRONMENT Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing in 5  day(s) LECTURER - SCHOOL OF DESIGN & ENVIRONMENT Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 08 Nov 2026 LECTURER, BIOMEDICAL ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 08 Nov 2026 LECTURER, ENGINEERING SCIENCE - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 08 Nov 2026 School of Infocomm - Lecturer (Common Infocomm Programme) Republic Polytechnic Closing in 2  day(s) ASSOCIATE LECTURER - STUDENT & YOUTH CARE SECTOR - HMIS Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing in 5  day(s) APPLY NOW"
    },
    "https://www.careers.hrp.gov.sg/sap/bc/ui5_ui5/sap/ZGERCFA004/index.html?search-keyword=Ngee%20Ann%20Polytechnic#/JobDescription/18151040/005056a3-d347-1fe1-b29a-c530e89642c3": {
      "title": "Manager (Safety, Security & Resilience) - Ees Office",
      "description": "Closing Date: 05/11/2026 Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button MANAGER (SAFETY, SECURITY & RESILIENCE) - EES OFFICE Ngee Ann Polytechnic 06-08 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time Closing in 5  day(s) 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is This is a 2-year contract position with the Estate, Eco & Safety Office. The Manager (Safety, Security and Resilience) plays a key role in protecting the Polytechnic's people, assets and operations. The incumbent will oversee campus security operations, emergency preparedness, crisis management, business continuity planning and technology-enabled security systems while supporting the development of an integrated and resilient campus environment. What you will be working on The Manager (Safety, Security and Resilience) will support the leadership and management of campus-wide safety, security and resilience programmes. Safety, Security and Resilience Manage and review campus security policies, procedures and operational frameworks. Oversee outsourced security operations and ensure service providers meet contractual and performance requirements. Manage security systems including CCTV, access control, intrusion detection, intercom and related technologies. Conduct security risk assessments and implement mitigation measures to address emerging threats. Lead investigations into security incidents, breaches and operational disruptions, and recommend corrective actions. Develop and coordinate emergency preparedness exercises, evacuation drills and crisis response programmes. Support the development, testing and continual improvement of Business Continuity Plans (BCP). Work closely with internal stakeholders and external agencies on safety, security and emergency-related matters. Support SGSecure initiatives and campus resilience programmes. Integrated Operations and Smart Security Support the development and operation of the Integrated Operations Centre (IOC). Leverage technology, analytics and digital monitoring platforms to enhance situational awareness and operational effectiveness. Monitor security trends, emerging technologies and industry best practices to improve campus security and resilience. Analyse operational and incident data and recommend improvement initiatives. Governance and Compliance Ensure compliance with relevant legislation, regulatory requirements, institutional policies and audit requirements. Support fire safety governance, security audits and operational reviews. Prepare reports, management papers and presentations for senior management and relevant committees. Stakeholder and Project Management Manage security-related projects, technology upgrades and operational improvement initiatives. Coordinate security arrangements for major events, VIP visits and special campus activities. Collaborate with Facilities Management, Safety, IT and other departments to support integrated campus operations. What we are looking for Knowledge in Security Management, Facilities Management, Engineering, Business, Risk Management or related discipline. At least 5 years of relevant experience in security management, emergency preparedness, resilience planning, facilities management or related fields. Experience managing outsourced security contracts and vendor performance. Familiarity with emergency response frameworks and relevant regulatory requirements. Experience in higher education, healthcare institutions, government agencies or multi-building institutional environment would be advantageous. Preferred Attributes Strong analytical, communication and stakeholder management skills. Ability to lead incident investigations and coordinate multi-agency responses. Experience in crisis management, business continuity planning or operational resilience programmes is an advantage. Familiarity with smart security technologies, command centres, integrated monitoring systems or IOC environments is preferred. Ability to manage projects and lead change initiatives across multiple stakeholders. About Ngee Ann Polytechnic At Ngee Ann Polytechnic, our nine academic schools offer over 40 full-time diplomas to a growing student population of more than 15,000. As a public tertiary institution, internationally-recognised for its academic excellence and close industry links, NP prides itself on having a dedicated and professional teaching faculty, complete with campus facilities that are among the finest in the world.\n\nAn institution of higher learning, Ngee Ann Polytechnic believes in giving every student an enriching learning experience and every employee the opportunity to build a meaningful career.\n\nIf you are a self-starter with an innovative mind, a versatile person with the drive for all-rounded excellence, and a dedicated team player who shares our vision and values, we invite you to join our inspired team. You might also be interested in Executive/Senior Project Manager (Project Management Department-EUP) Building And Construction Authority Closing on 05 Nov 2026 Assistant Manager, Land Dealings Approval Unit (LDAU) Singapore Land Authority Closing on 05 Nov 2026 Senior Manager, Centre Management Singapore Land Authority Closing on 08 Nov 2026 Facilities Manager  (Integrated Development) Singapore Land Authority Closing on 08 Nov 2026 Executive/Senior Executive - Eco-Campus Solutions & Services Dept Nanyang Polytechnic Closing on 22 Nov 2026 Assistant Director (Facilities Management) People'S Association Closing on 08 Nov 2026 Manager (Valuer, Property Tax Division) Inland Revenue Authority Of Singapore Closing on 08 Nov 2026 Assistant Manager (O&M Design) JTC Corporation Closing on 07 Nov 2026 MANAGER (SAFETY, SECURITY & RESILIENCE) - EES OFFICE Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing in 5  day(s) APPLY NOW"
    },
    "https://www.careers.hrp.gov.sg/sap/bc/ui5_ui5/sap/ZGERCFA004/index.html?search-keyword=Ngee%20Ann%20Polytechnic#/JobDescription/18183960/005056a3-53e2-1fd1-b4e1-a481ccd8140d": {
      "title": "Lecturer - School Of Design & Environment",
      "description": "Closing Date: 15/11/2026 Find A Job | Careers@Gov Emphasized Available Values Footer actions skip to content Home Find A Job/ Internship FAQ CONTACT US LOGIN LOG OUT menu-button search-button LECTURER - SCHOOL OF DESIGN & ENVIRONMENT Ngee Ann Polytechnic 03-05 year(s) Fixed Terms, Full-time Closing on 15 Nov 2026 0 Applicant(s) APPLY NOW What the role is This is a 2-year contract position as a Lecturer in the School of Design & Environment. What you will be working on Academic duties Develop and improve the content of modules you are assigned to teach and deliver for full-time and part-time learners Be competent to conduct teaching and delivery of modules in classroom and online setting Set and conduct assessments for the modules you are assigned Lead in the integration of modules content, teaching and delivery to achieve the course objectives Initiate and experiment with new pedagogies or learning technologies to enhance curriculum delivery Non-Academic duties Administrative and other duties to support the management of the school, diploma and modules Duties and responsibilities that may arises to support curriculum development and currency Solve operational problems to ensure efficiency and effectiveness Supervise junior team members to ensure smooth operations What we are looking for Applicants must have strong communication skills and have an inherent passion to teach students in both physical classrooms and online learning environment. Candidate should have at least 3 years of demonstrated experience and be competent to plan, develop and teach at least three of the following areas: Fire Safety Management Mechanical Facilities Property Management Customer Experience Management Project Planning & Management Smart & Green Building Management Besides teaching full time diploma students, the lecturer will also be required to teach Part-Time Courses to learners who are working adults. These classes are usually conducted in the evenings from 6pm to 10pm. About Ngee Ann Polytechnic At Ngee Ann Polytechnic, our nine academic schools offer over 40 full-time diplomas to a growing student population of more than 15,000. As a public tertiary institution, internationally-recognised for its academic excellence and close industry links, NP prides itself on having a dedicated and professional teaching faculty, complete with campus facilities that are among the finest in the world.\n\nAn institution of higher learning, Ngee Ann Polytechnic believes in giving every student an enriching learning experience and every employee the opportunity to build a meaningful career.\n\nIf you are a self-starter with an innovative mind, a versatile person with the drive for all-rounded excellence, and a dedicated team player who shares our vision and values, we invite you to join our inspired team. You might also be interested in LECTURER - SCHOOL OF DESIGN & ENVIRONMENT Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 08 Nov 2026 LECTURER, BIOMEDICAL ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 08 Nov 2026 LECTURER, ENGINEERING SCIENCE - SCHOOL OF ENGINEERING Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 08 Nov 2026 LECTURER, DESIGN  - SCHOOL OF DESIGN & ENVIRONMENT Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing in 4  day(s) LECTURER, CIVIL ENGINEERING - SCHOOL OF DESIGN & ENVIRONMENT Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 15 Nov 2026 SERVICE-LEARNING CATALYST, LECTURER - HMIS Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 15 Nov 2026 ASSOCIATE LECTURER - STUDENT & YOUTH CARE SECTOR - HMIS Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing in 4  day(s) School of Hospitality - Lecturer (Events & Project Management) Republic Polytechnic Closing in 1  day(s) LECTURER - SCHOOL OF DESIGN & ENVIRONMENT Ngee Ann Polytechnic Closing on 15 Nov 2026 APPLY NOW"
    },
